    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n52631" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλλιγρᾰφ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>write beautifully</i>, in point of style, metaph.in 
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. τὴν ἀπομίμησιν τοῖς τῆς ἀρετῆς
					στοιχείοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh.Al.</u>
					1420b17
				</span></i>
			: pf.
			
				Pass.
			 in act. sense, <i><span class="en">
				Longin.
				33.5
			</span></i>; in pass. sense, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεκαλλιγραφημένοι λόγοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					2.31
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				7.18
			</span></i>: later use for 
				Att.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς κάλλος γράφειν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				99
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>paint beautifully</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ πρόσωπον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					5.102
				</span></i>
			.</div>
